<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shunten</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shunten is the legendary first king of Ryukyu, said in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chuzan-seikan">Chūzan Seikan</a> chronicle to have reigned from 1187 to 1237. Later tradition made him a son of the Japanese warrior Minamoto no Tametomo and a local woman, a story used to tie the Ryukyuan royal line to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. His dynasty was said to have ended with his grandson, after whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eiso">Eiso</a> took power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shunten.jpg" alt="Shunten" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Katsushika Hokusai · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chinsetsu_Yumiharizuki_28-6_the_enthronement_of_Sutemaru_Cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Its early seat was Urasoe castle, and its rulers claimed descent from earlier legendary dynasties of <b>Shunten</b> and Eiso.</blockquote><a href="/state/chuzan">Chuzan</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urasoe">Urasoe</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=26.25,127.72" aria-label="Urasoe on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7922 1200 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Shunten"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8372 1470h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8372 1470h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=26.25,127.72">What was here? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
